WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.988
Now the code.

2
00:00:00.988 --> 00:00:06.251
It's one PowerShell module, two entry
scripts, the call list and the tier map.

3
00:00:06.251 --> 00:00:10.580
Every call goes through one reader,
built for one task in one cloud,

4
00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:15.712
and the only thing that touches the network
is a small script block you hand it:

5
00:00:15.712 --> 00:00:19.000
a live one for real runs, or
a fake for labs and tests.

6
00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:22.325
The reader enforces four
rules, shown on the slide.

7
00:00:22.325 --> 00:00:25.771
It only makes calls the
task declares, only reads,

8
00:00:25.771 --> 00:00:31.180
only sends its token to the cloud's own
host, and always reads to the last page.
